== 7.1 Classifying Games

Games can be described by their equipment, setting, number of participants or objective. *Football* and *basketball* are commonly played as team games with a ball. *Badminton* uses rackets and a shuttlecock; *table tennis* uses paddles or rackets and a lightweight ball on a table. These categories can overlap: a game may be both a racket game and a doubles game.

A game's detailed rules depend on its governing code and competition. This chapter introduces the activity and its skills rather than asserting that every local or modified game uses the same dimensions, player numbers or regulations as an international competition.

